From: Panurus maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] zeroize prover secrets

- bytes_clear writes through a volatile pointer: on macOS explicit_bzero is
  #defined to bzero, which the compiler may drop before a free;
- poly_wipe / polyvec_wipe / polymat_wipe zero the coefficient limbs and the
  CRT representation of a secret before it is freed;
- the LNP prover wipes its witness (s1, s2, m) in lin_prover_clear and the
  temporary copies made by lin_prover_set_witness, and the prove functions
  wipe the expanded prover randomness and the internally generated coins.

Panurus-local patch, applied by `make lazer-install` (lazer.mk).

diff --git a/src/bytes.c b/src/bytes.c
index 2d8402c..a6ac8b7 100644
--- a/src/bytes.c
+++ b/src/bytes.c
@@ -91,7 +91,18 @@ bytes_inp_raw (uint8_t *bytes, size_t len, FILE *stream)
 void
 bytes_clear (uint8_t *bytes, const size_t nbytes)
 {
-  explicit_bzero (bytes, nbytes);
+  /*
+   * On macOS explicit_bzero is defined to bzero, which the compiler may
+   * elide before a free: write through a volatile pointer instead
+   * (panurus patch).
+   */
+  volatile uint8_t *p = bytes;
+  size_t i;
+
+  if (bytes == NULL)
+    return;
+  for (i = 0; i < nbytes; i++)
+    p[i] = 0;
 }
 
 static inline int
